menu "Home Assistant (MQTT)"

    config HA_MQTT_ENABLE
        bool "Publish the board to Home Assistant over MQTT"
        default n
        help
            Publish the board to an MQTT broker with Home Assistant discovery:
            one device with sensors, switches and buttons, and a short list
            of commands it accepts. The broker and its login are set on
            General Settings. Nothing runs, and no RAM is used, until MQTT is
            turned on there. Plain MQTT only (no TLS), port 1883 by default.

    config HA_MQTT_DISCOVERY_PREFIX
        string "Home Assistant discovery prefix"
        default "homeassistant"
        depends on HA_MQTT_ENABLE
        help
            The topic Home Assistant watches for discovery messages. The
            board also listens on <prefix>/status for Home Assistant's
            "online" message. That topic is a separate Home Assistant setting
            (default homeassistant/status): change both if you change this.
            Missing it only delays updates, since every topic is retained.

endmenu
